# Environment & deployment

## Local development (maintainers)

```bash
# From repo root: Postgres in Docker
docker compose up -d db

# In WSL, project directory:
wasp db migrate-dev
wasp start
```

- **Dev Docker = PostgreSQL only** (`docker-compose.yml` service `db`). App = **Wasp CLI in WSL**.
- `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.server` (see `.env.server.example`). Never commit secrets or private `Bankauszüge/` data.

## Shipping / end-user run (full Docker stack)

- Spec: [`ai/docs/shipping-plan.md`](mdc:ai/docs/shipping-plan.md) · setup (GitHub root): [`README.md`](mdc:README.md)
- Stack: `docker-compose.ship.yml` + `ship/Dockerfile` — **db + server + client** all in containers
- Host needs **Docker Desktop + Git only** (no WSL/Node/Wasp for recipients)
- Bind **`127.0.0.1` only**; URL `http://zastermaster` (hosts + port 80; fallback `3080`)
- Scripts: `start.bat` / `stop.bat` / `update.bat` / `backup.bat` / `setup-hosts.bat`
- Separate Compose project + volume from dev — **does not wipe** `zastermaster_pgdata`
- Trying ship on a maintainer PC: ship API is **`3002`** (wasp stays on `3001`); `start.bat` / `stop.bat`
- Do **not** replace the WSL dev workflow with ship Compose for day-to-day coding

## Do not

- Suggest installing Wasp on native Windows for **recipients** (ship builds inside Docker)
- Put the whole Wasp app in Docker for **normal maintainer dev** (keep `wasp start` + db-only Compose)
- Cloud-host bank data or commit `.env.ship` / `Bankauszüge/`
